WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.053 --> 00:00:01.080
(soft percussive music)

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:03.120
- [Reporter] A record number
of young people in China

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.700
graduated from college this year,

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.231
but instead of celebrating...

00:00:07.231 --> 00:00:08.370
(camera shutter clicking)

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:11.310
Some are marking the
milestone on social media

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:15.030
by lying down flat on the ground
in their graduation gowns,

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.940
looking dejected and exhausted.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.490
After studying for
years, they're frustrated

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:22.740
with the struggle to find decent work

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:26.730
as China's youth unemployment
rate hits historic highs.

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:29.280
So for some, the better option for now

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:33.120
is to stay at home as
so-called full-time children.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.340
- If you have a lot of idle young people

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:38.760
who are not employed, it adds
pressure on social stability

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:41.850
which is what the government
really is concerned about.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.440
- [Reporter] Here's
why millions of Chinese

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.393
graduates are out of work.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.140
The term full-time children has gone viral

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.000
on Chinese social media.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.160
Videos show young people spending time

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.470
with their parents, cooking and cleaning

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:57.273
in exchange for a salary.

00:00:57.273 --> 00:01:00.150
(son speaks Chinese)

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:03.360
- They are choosing to
stay at home full time.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:05.370
They are counting on their parents

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:07.710
to continue support them financially.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:10.080
This is what many people are referring to

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:13.230
as the 'lying flat' phenomenon In China

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:15.090
- [Reporter] Lying flat essentially means

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:17.370
to resist the intense social pressure

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:20.403
to study hard and work even harder.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.990
A record 11.6 million young Chinese

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:27.180
graduated from college this year,

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:30.720
almost 12 times more than 20 years ago.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.910
- Students, they have
much higher expectation

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:36.900
for their job income, their job stability,

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.140
and what they can derive by doing work.

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.580
- [Reporter] But the graduates soon found,

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.920
they're competing with thousands of others

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.690
for only a handful of jobs

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:48.720
that match their skills and expectations.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:53.720
Urban youth unemployment
hit a record 21.3% in June.

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:57.720
Joblessness in China increased
dramatically in recent years

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.870
while other countries such
as the U.S. saw a spike

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:03.150
in youth unemployment during the pandemic

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:06.240
that rapidly fell as
restrictions were eased.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:08.520
China maintained COVID controls for longer

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.520
than most countries,
keeping its borders closed

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:14.370
from 2020 to early 2023.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:16.950
Major cities went through
extended lockdowns

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.200
that disrupted production.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.740
As the economy slowed, so too, did hiring.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:24.900
China's youth unemployment rates rose

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:27.450
for six consecutive months this year.

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:30.390
Then in August, the
government abruptly announced

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:32.700
that it would stop reporting that data,

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:35.640
citing plans to revisit the methodology.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:38.430
Analysts say the suspension
fits a worrying pattern

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:42.003
of haziness around the true
state of China's economy.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.780
To address the youth unemployment problem,

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.330
local governments ordered
state-owned companies

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:50.670
to hire more graduates.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.050
They're also pushing young people

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:54.120
to take up blue-collared work,

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:57.270
but that's unappealing for
a lot of college graduates.

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:59.490
A survey from online recruitment platform,

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:02.760
Zhaopin, found that a quarter
of this year's graduates

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.680
want to work in the technology sector,

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:07.530
despite the fact that some
of China's biggest tech firms

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:10.230
had massive layoffs following a regulatory

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:12.210
crackdown on the industry.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:15.090
- [Stella Xie] So unless
confidence revive in those sectors,

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:18.270
young college graduates will
likely continue to struggle

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:21.303
in terms of what kind of work
they're looking for to do.

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:25.020
- Down the line, having
millions of young people

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.850
out of work will have serious

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:29.100
ripple effects for China's society.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.470
- High jobless rate among young people

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:34.650
also exacerbate many other
structural challenges

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:36.240
that China already is dealing with.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:38.790
For example, without stable jobs,

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:41.790
many people are putting
off getting married.

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:45.360
They don't wanna have kids,
and all these will make

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:48.930
China's demographic situation even worse.

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:51.870
- [Reporter] Some are
warning of a lost generation.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:54.720
It's adding to a long list
of challenges for Beijing

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:57.660
to boost growth and
attract foreign investors

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:59.730
as the world's second largest economy

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:02.383
tries to rebuild from the pandemic.

00:04:02.383 --> 00:04:04.800
(soft music)

